---
import { BRAND } from '@truecontact/shared';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy policy — ${BRAND.name}`}
  description="What TrueContact and its WhatsApp connector do with your data."
>
  <main class="wrap narrow section">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy policy</p>
    <h1>Your data stays yours.</h1>
    <p class="section-lede">
      {BRAND.name} is a personal contact book that gathers observations from the sources you
      connect — a WhatsApp connector and vCard/CSV files you choose to import. This page explains
      exactly what is stored and where it goes.
    </p>

    <h2>What TrueContact stores</h2>
    <ul class="ticks ticks--yes">
      <li>Your account details: email address and name.</li>
      <li>
        The contacts you import — names, phone numbers, emails, and notes — together with the
        history of what changed and which source it came from.
      </li>
      <li>
        Import files are kept only while an import is processed; the durable record is your
        contact graph and its history.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The WhatsApp connector</h2>
    <ul class="ticks ticks--yes">
      <li>
        It reads contact information WhatsApp Web already displays (names, chat identifiers, and
        phone numbers where WhatsApp shows them) and sends it to <em>your</em> {BRAND.name}
        account over HTTPS.
      </li>
      <li>
        It never asks for, sees, or stores your WhatsApp password, OTPs, or session secrets, and
        it does not read your messages.
      </li>
      <li>
        It stores a {BRAND.name}-issued pairing token in your browser so it can push updates; you
        can disconnect it at any time from the extension.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we never do</h2>
    <ul class="ticks ticks--no">
      <li>Sell your contact data or use it for advertising.</li>
      <li>Hand your data to third parties — it lives on our hosting provider and nowhere else.</li>
      <li>Change your canonical contacts without your explicit decision in the app.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Export and deletion</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      You can export your whole contact book as vCard or CSV at any time, and you can delete all of
      your contact data from the app itself — Imports → <strong>Delete all data</strong>. Account
      deletion is also available by opening an issue in the project repository.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      The web app uses a single session cookie so you stay signed in. There are no analytics,
      tracking, or advertising cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Questions or deletion requests: open an issue at
      <a href="https://github.com/PrakashSewani/true-contact/issues">
        github.com/PrakashSewani/true-contact
      </a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
